; One executable per module under test; they all share the Support fixtures
; and testables. Framebuffer (a wrapper over an SDL texture) and Renderer
; (per-pixel SDL output) need a live SDL surface, so their pure pieces are
; tested through Plane, Viewport, Material and Atmosphere instead. Input reads
; SDL for the keyboard and the mouse, but its edges and hold timer are a pure
; function of two frames and a duration, and test_input drives that directly.
;
; tsdl is a direct dependency here because naming a key is naming an
; Sdl.Scancode — the same way a game binding one has to.
;
; The demo's suites live here too, beside the engine's own, because they share
; these fixtures and there is no reason to run them separately. A game built on
; this engine tests itself in its own repo.

; The suites that load pictures read them from fixtures/ by plain relative
; path, because dune runs a test with its working directory here — so the
; loaders are tested without going through Asset, and Asset is tested without
; going near SDL. The demos' own art comes in through Asset, which is why the
; whole of assets/ is a dependency too: test_demos builds every demo's world,
; and one of them reads files.

(tests
 (deps
  (glob_files fixtures/*)
  (source_tree ../assets))
 (names
  test_vec
  test_result_ext
  test_asset
  test_surface
  test_plane
  test_sky
  test_image
  test_transform
  test_room
  test_world
  test_ray
  test_player
  test_viewport
  test_color
  test_texture
  test_material
  test_atmosphere
  test_input
  test_sight
  test_engine
  test_patterns
  test_pictures
  test_level
  test_demos)
 (libraries raycaster camlcast_demo alcotest tsdl))
